WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.700
Open Campaigns to see the Meta campaigns you’ve synced.

00:03.700 --> 00:05.800
Pick the one you want to review and click Run check.

00:05.800 --> 00:08.200
The report shows what passed and what needs attention.

00:08.200 --> 00:11.000
It checks whether the landing page loads,

00:11.000 --> 00:13.000
how quickly the server responds,

00:13.000 --> 00:16.000
and whether the ad copy has spelling or grammar issues.

00:16.000 --> 00:19.000
Here, it suggests a correction for a French typo.

00:19.000 --> 00:20.500
That’s just a sample.

00:20.500 --> 00:23.000
You’ll find many more checks in the full report.

00:23.000 --> 00:27.000
Click Start watch to keep checking the campaign’s destination.

00:27.000 --> 00:29.500
Campaign Watch checks your landing pages

00:29.500 --> 00:32.000
every 30 minutes to see if they’re still up.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.000
Here, a page returned a 404,

00:36.000 --> 00:38.500
so it shows up as an incident.

00:38.500 --> 00:43.000
In Settings, you can turn on email alerts for new incidents.

00:43.000 --> 00:46.500
You can also enable automatic pausing

00:46.500 --> 00:49.000
for active campaigns on watch

00:49.000 --> 00:52.000
after repeated, confirmed page failures.

00:52.000 --> 00:56.880
Start your free preview at clickcohere.com.
